%% A business analyst signs in to the Data Analytics Engine through Keycloak brokered to Entra ID, then queries a governed table (SEC-01, LAK-09). Sample.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as Finance analyst
  participant T as Data Analytics Engine<br/>(Trino / Starburst)
  participant K as Keycloak<br/>realm aidp-prod
  participant E as Entra ID
  participant AC as Trino access rules
  participant LOG as SIEM
  U->>T: Open web UI or JDBC (externalAuthentication)
  T-->>U: Redirect to Keycloak (authorization code + PKCE)
  U->>K: Authorize, client = trino
  K-->>U: Redirect to Entra ID (identity brokering)
  U->>E: Sign in with password + MFA
  E-->>K: ID token (upn, object id)
  K->>K: First-broker-login links the user, reads AD groups via LDAP federation
  K-->>U: Authorization code
  U->>T: Code
  T->>K: Exchange code for tokens (client secret)
  K-->>T: Access token: preferred_username, groups = [aidp-prod-finance-reader], aud = trino
  T->>T: Validate signature (JWKS), issuer, audience, expiry
  U->>T: SELECT from iceberg.prod_finance_consumption.revenue_by_region_month
  T->>AC: user + groups
  AC-->>T: allow SELECT, mask PII columns
  T-->>U: Rows
  K->>LOG: LOGIN, CODE_TO_TOKEN events
  T->>LOG: Query event with user and groups
